      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Island instead of Seat of the Synod is suboptimal. Seat of the Synod is an artifact land that counts toward Metalcraft for Mox Opal. With Seat of the Synod + Lotus Petal + Mox Opal (or two Mox Opals + Seat), the player can activate Metalcraft with 3 artifacts, enabling Mox Opal to tap for mana. Playing Island instead means one fewer artifact on board, making it harder to reach Metalcraft. Since the player has two Mox Opals, Lotus Petal, Urza's Bauble, and Seat of the Synod, playing Seat as the land maximizes artifact count and enables Metalcraft immediately (Seat + any two of Mox Opal/Lotus Petal/Urza's Bauble = 3 artifacts). The Island provides no artifact synergy benefit. The player can still play Seat of the Synod later, but they only get one land drop per turn, and saving Island for a future turn (or not needing it) while getting the artifact land down now is clearly better sequencing.",
