      "description": "Kimi25 Analyst declined to counter Prismatic Ending, which exiled Chalice of the Void. Chalice on 1 was a key lock piece that had been countering Grok4F Timmy's 1-mana spells (Ponder, Brainstorm, Swords to Plowshares, Stern Scolding) all game. Losing Chalice frees the opponent to cast all their powerful 1-mana cantrips and removal. Kimi25 had two copies of Force of Will in hand and could exile one to the other to counter the Prismatic Ending for free (paying 1 life). The reasoning mentions 'save my countermagic for any threats they play' but Chalice of the Void IS the threat — it's the prison piece locking the opponent out. Protecting it is far more valuable than holding Force of Will for a hypothetical future spell, especially when the opponent's graveyard shows they're full of 1-mana spells that Chalice was blanking.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Prismatic Ending, allowing Chalice of the Void to be exiled.",
      "better_line": "Cast Force of Will (exiling the other Force of Will as the blue card, paying 1 life) to counter Prismatic Ending and preserve Chalice of the Void, which was locking the opponent out of most of their spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 106,
      "player": "Kimi25 Analyst",
      "decision_index": 125,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Targeted Mox Opal with Emry's ability, but there's already a Mox Opal on the battlefield. Casting a second legendary Mox Opal means one gets sacrificed to the legend rule, providing no lasting board advantage beyond a Patchwork Automaton trigger. Lotus Petal would provide the same Automaton trigger plus a mana of any color when sacrificed.",
